# apps/web's build settings for prod, which `make -C infra web-build` reads before `bun run build`
# (dl-e8ov.2.64). Nothing here is secret: the browser holds all of it. This file wins over your
# shell, so a build has exactly what is written here, and an empty value means none.
#
# Sign-in stays off in prod until the consent text (dl-e8ov.2.9) lands. With JW_SUPABASE_URL or
# JW_SUPABASE_KEY empty, the bundle has no sign-in at all (apps/web/src/config.ts authConfig).
# Turning it on is then:
#   JW_SUPABASE_URL=https://auth.jadwigo.pl   once the custom domain is active (dl-e8ov.2.65)
#   JW_SUPABASE_KEY=<jadwigo-prod's publishable key>
# JW_SUPABASE_PROVIDERS is a comma list of the buttons shown: google, facebook. It stays empty until
# dl-e8ov.2.8 (Google) and dl-e8ov.2.58 (Facebook) switch each one on.
JW_SUPABASE_URL=
JW_SUPABASE_KEY=
JW_SUPABASE_PROVIDERS=
